The root cause of the "wonky" selection behavior lies in the `toggleSelection` function in `renamer-browser/static/js/app.js`.

**Root Cause:**
In single-select mode (default), the function clears all selections *before* checking if the current item is selected.
```javascript
if (!state.multiSelect) {
    state.selected.clear(); // 1. Selection cleared (Set is empty)
}
if (state.selected.has(path)) { // 2. Always returns false!
    state.selected.delete(path);
} else {
    state.selected.add(path); // 3. Always adds the item back
}
```
This means:
1.  **You cannot deselect an item:** Clicking a selected item clears it and immediately re-selects it.
2.  **Navigation behavior:** When you navigate to a new image and select it, the previous image is deselected (because `state.selected.clear()` runs). When you return, it is correctly shown as unselected. This is intended behavior for single-select mode, but combined with the inability to deselect, it feels broken.

**Plan:**
Refactor `toggleSelection` to capture the selection state *before* clearing the set.

```javascript
function toggleSelection(path) {
    const wasSelected = state.selected.has(path);

    if (!state.multiSelect) {
        state.selected.clear();
        // If it wasn't selected before, select it now.
        // If it WAS selected, we effectively deselected it by clearing.
        if (!wasSelected) {
            state.selected.add(path);
        }
    } else {
        if (wasSelected) {
            state.selected.delete(path);
        } else {
            state.selected.add(path);
        }
    }
    // ... update UI ...
}
```

**Risks:**
-   None identified. This restores standard toggle logic.

